  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nWarming trend back to well above normal temperatures next week:\n\nGlobal ensembles are then coming into better agreement on a slow\nwave progression of a digging trough/low over the SW CONUS. This\nwill lead to a prolonged amplified ridging pattern over our\narea, renewing southerly surface flow, keeping weather dry, and\ninitiating a warming trend to well above normal temperatures by\nthe middle of next week. Highs Monday are forecast to be around\n70 F, with highs reaching the lower 80s by Wednesday and \nThursday. For context, normal highs for that time of year are in\nthe upper 60s.\n\nCurrently, October (MTD) is the 2nd warmest on record, coming\noff of the warmest ever September on record. While the cool\ntemperatures this weekend will put a dent in that placement, a\nreturn to persistent above normal temperatures will likely keep\nthis October ranked amongst some of the warmest.",
